\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Karen Weise, The Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 498 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 February 2022\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Workplace\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  Tells Workers\par \par \uc2 To Return to Office Soon\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  told employees that they will need to return to office next month, transitioning back to its corporate campus for the first time since the Omicron coronavirus variant tore through the nation.\par \par \uc2 The company has long said it would embrace a hybrid work environment, with most employees able to work from home up to 50 percent of the time. In a Monday morning blog post focused on its headquarters near Seattle, \uc2 Chris Capossela\uc2 , an executive, said that starting Feb. 28, ''employees will have 30 days to make adjustments to their routines and adopt the working preferences they've agreed upon with their managers.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Capossela cited the high vaccination rates in King County, where most employees live, and declining hospitalizations and deaths in the state as factors in the decision.\par \par \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  was the first major employer to shutter its offices in March 2020. KAREN WEISE\par \par \uc2 REGIONAL\par \par \uc2 Maine Lobstermen Bounced Back in 2021\par \par \uc2 Maine's lobster industry bounced back in 2021 and set a record $725 million for the total value of lobsters brought to the docks, and which was over $300 million more than 2020, state regulators said Monday.\par \par \uc2 The state's lobster fishing business, by far the largest of its kind in the U.S., dipped below 100 million pounds of catch in 2020 for the first time in nearly a decade and brought in around $412 million. In 2021, about 108 million pounds were caught, the most since 2018, the \uc2 Maine Department of Marine Resources\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The lobsters were also worth more; last year's $725 million eclipsed the previous record of about $541 million in 2016.\par \par \uc2 The per-pound price of lobster soared in 2021, which contributed to the record high value. The price to fishermen at the docks rose to $6.71 per pound, an increase of about 60 percent from 2020 and easily a state record. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 ADVERTISING\par \par \uc2 Polestar's Super Bowl Ad Ribbing Musk Won the Day\par \par \uc2 A Leonardo DiCaprio-backed Polestar ad taking a potshot at rivals \uc2 Tesla\uc2  and \uc2 Volkswagen\uc2  topped the list of the most popular commercials during Super Bowl LVI, new data on Monday showed.\par \par \uc2 The 30-second ad by the electric-car maker performed roughly 23 times better than other commercials aired during the game, according to consumer search data firm EDO, with its message of ''no epic voiceovers,'' ''no empty promises,'' and ''no hidden agendas'' aiming squarely at the idea of conquering Mars as well as the Volkswagen Dieselgate.\par \par \uc2 Polestar, which is owned by China's Geely and \uc2 Volvo Cars\uc2 , is in the process of going public through a reverse merger with special-purpose acquisition company (SPAC) Gores Guggenheim in the first half of 2022.\par \par \uc2 Tesla\uc2  boss \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  responded with a laugh emoji on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , when one of his nearly 74 million followers pointed to the Polestar ad. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPHS BY AP) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020220215ei2f00055\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
