\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Todd Gregory, Ceylan Yeginsu, Oscar Lopez and Lananh Nguyen \par \uc2 610 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 December 2021\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRAVEL\par \par \uc2 C.D.C. Tells Travelers to Avoid Cruise Ships\par \par \uc2 The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  on Thursday raised its Covid-19 warning level for cruise ships to 4, the highest, and issued a blunt warning: ''Avoid cruise travel regardless of vaccination status.''\par \par \uc2 The move came as the number of outbreaks on ships has grown in recent weeks, causing some ports to turn away ships. Last week, dozens of people on a \uc2 Royal Caribbean International\uc2  ship tested positive after it set sail from Fort Lauderdale, Fla., and a Carnival Cruise Line ship returned to Miami on Sunday after positive tests among ''a small number on board.''\par \par \uc2 Calling the C.D.C.'s decision ''perplexing,'' the cruise industry's trade group, \uc2 Cruise Lines International Association\uc2 , said in a statement that the number of cases onboard made up a slim minority of the total population and that ''the majority of cases were asymptomatic or mild in nature, posing little to no burden on medical resources onboard or onshore.''\par \par \uc2 Before the C.D.C.'s warning, \uc2 Royal Caribbean Group\uc2 , one of the biggest cruise companies, said its ships had carried 1.1 million guests since it had restarted U.S. operations in June, with 1,745 people testing positive. While the majority of passengers had mild or no symptoms, 41 people were hospitalized.\par \par \uc2 The coronavirus wreaked havoc on the cruise industry in the early stages of the pandemic, infecting hundreds of cruise passengers and workers and requiring the sector to shut down for 18 months. To begin sailing, cruise ships had to agree to the C.D.C.'s Conditional Sailing Order, which is valid until Jan. 15.\par \par \uc2 Most cruise companies do not publicly announce the number of coronavirus cases identified during sailings, but all cruise ships operating to and from U.S. ports must submit daily numbers to the C.D.C., which uses a color-coded system to inform the public whether the number of cases is above or below the agency's threshold for an investigation.\par \par \uc2 Currently 88 cruise ships are being monitored by the C.D.C. because of reported coronavirus cases onboard. The agency does not publicly specify the number of cases on each ship. TODD GREGORY, CEYLAN YEGINSU and OSCAR LOPEZ\par \par \uc2 BANKS\par \par \uc2 Citi Tells Its Employees to Work From Home\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  has expanded remote working for its U.S. employees as a surge in coronavirus cases disrupts Wall Street's return-to-office plans. Again.\par \par \uc2 ''We are asking that you work from home for the first few weeks of the new year if you are able to do so,'' \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  said in a memo to staff on Thursday. ''We will continue to monitor the data and provide an update in January on when we expect to be back in the office.''\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 's new guidance applies to employees in more than 30 offices around the country who had been called back since September. Employees in New York City and New Jersey were already given the option to work from home in the final weeks of the year.\par \par \uc2 JPMorgan Chase\uc2  gave employees more flexibility to work from home in the first two weeks of January, but expects them to return to in-office schedules no later than Feb. 1, according to a memo to employees.\par \par \uc2 ''We are not changing our longterm plans of working in the office,'' the bank's operating committee said in the memo. The company may also amend its policy on vaccinations, which it has not required so far. LANANH NGUYEN\par \par \uc2 (PHOTOGRAPH BY CHANDAN KHANNA/AFP -- GETTY IMAGES) \par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020211231ehcv0004e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
